\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Turkey - Feb 21. \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2003\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ANKARA, Feb 21 (Reuters) - These are the leading stories in the Turkish press on Friday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  SABAH \par \par \uc2  - Bush's hand is tied: Turkey's determined bargaining over opening its bases to U.S. troops reflects how important a northern front against Iraq is in any war. \par \par \uc2  ZAMAN \par \par \uc2  - Even the weather conditions mean the United States must open a northern front against Iraq if it launches a war. The wind in southern Iraq during the 1991 Gulf War sickened U.S. troops and damaged equipment, including tanks. \par \par \uc2  RADIKAL \par \par \uc2  - Talks are in deadlock: The government doesn't send a request for the approval of the troop deployment to parliament; Washington temporarily suspends talks. \par \par \uc2  - Governing Justice and Development Party leader Tayyip Erdogan's five-year political ban ends with a High Election Board decision to let him run in an upcoming by-election. \par \par \uc2  MILLIYET \par \par \uc2  - Prime Minister Abdullah Gul will announce his government's decision on the U.S. troop deployment on Friday after meeting the American ambassador. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Iraqi Kurds attempt to take the northern oil-rich cities of Mosul and Kirkuk. \par \par \uc2  HURRIYET \par \par \uc2  - The political and security makeup of a post-war Iraq dominates discussions between U.S. and Turkish officials. Iraq is to remain united and independent, and a central authority will control oil flows. Kurdish militias will be disarmed, and there will be one Iraqi army. \par \par \uc2  CUMHURIYET \par \par \uc2  - Turkey moves 7,000 troops into northern Iraq after reports Tehran has deployed 5,000 soldiers to the Kurdish enclave. \par \par \uc2  DUNYA \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sureyya Serdengecti says the impact of a short \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Iraq on the lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and inflation will not be long-term. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030221dz2l00dwe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
