\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Turkish CB defends lira as Iraq woes hit mkts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Gamze Alarslan \par \uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2002\par 16:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Dec 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the lira on Tuesday after it sank close to record lows on fears about a looming war in Iraq that could further damage Turkey's fragile economy. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the interbank market at around 1,697,000/1,699,000 to the dollar to support the flagging local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The lira hit an intra-day record low of 1,737,000 on November 4 before recovering to just above 1.5 million earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Concerns that a conflict next door could destabilise Turkey's fragile economy have sent the unit tumbling in recent days, alongside falling shares and debt prices. \par \par \uc2  The lira recovered to close at best bids of 1,676,000 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , still weaker than Monday's close of 1,650,000. \par \par \uc2  "We've been saying the lira should be falling, we've been saying it's overvalued," said Charles Robertson, emerging Europe economist at ING Baring. "It looks like the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is just trying to manage the decline." \par \par \uc2  The main share index  ended the day down 2.38 percent at 10,447.46 points, extending sharp losses over the past week as Washington edged closer to war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  But shares too closed off lows after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reassurances from Prime Minister Abdullah Gul that \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not gearing up for war. \par \par \uc2  "Any news on preparations for war is what's driving the market. Once we fell as far as 10,000 there was a slight reaction and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have had something to do with that," said Mustafa Karaca of Taksim Securities in Istanbul. \par \par \uc2  Benchmark December 3, 2003 debt was also weaker at yields of 58.01 percent from Monday's close of 56.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investors had largely withdrawn from the market ahead of the year-end and local players were also winding down business. \par \par \uc2  Turkey fears that war in Iraq could damage its fragile economic recovery and the IMF pact underpinning it, and could spread over Turkey's southern border. \par \par \uc2  A close U.S. ally, NATO member Turkey is expected to provide reluctant support if Washington strikes against Iraq for allegedly developing weapons of mass destruction. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Abdullah Gul told his party's lawmakers that the situation in Iraq had reached a "serious point" and Turkey could not remain indifferent. \par \par \uc2  Gul met senior advisors as well as the president and military chief on Monday night to discuss possible support for the United States and Tuesday's newspapers were full of speculation about what Ankara's role would be in any war. \par \par \uc2  A top Israeli general and an Iraqi Kurdish leader visited Ankara on Tuesday for talks. \par \par \uc2  "Even though it's been expected for a long time (dollar) prices have gone up because a war in Iraq is becoming more concrete," said one banker in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  In addition to Iraq fears, investors are also watching the government for progress on next year's budget and on reforms promised to the IMF in return for a latest $1.6 billion loan tranche due to be paid after a review in January. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021224dyco00n05\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
