\par\par \b \uc2  Turk CB says acted to help lira against Iraq worries. \b0\par\par\uc2 160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2002\par 13:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ANKARA, Dec 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prevent the lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losing value over worries about looming war in neighbouring Iraq. \par \par \uc2  "Extreme volatility has been seen in the exchange rate in recent days linked to increasing tension of a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  against Iraq," the bank said in a written statement. \par \par \uc2  "Today a direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the sale side was carried out against this extreme volatility," it said. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the bank stepped in to sell dollars for lira at around 1,697,000 lira to the dollar, driving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to around 1,683,500 on the interbank market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had strengthened to around 1.5 million to the dollar earlier this month on optimism for the new government. The bank stressed that it had no target value for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but wanted to prevent volatility. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021224dyco00m2h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
