\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Turk mkts fall on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 ,Iraq fears. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mark Bentley \par \uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2002\par 16:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lira fell against the dollar on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday to stabilise the unit which has rallied strongly since November 3 elections, threatening exports. \par \par \uc2  A landslide November election win for the Justice and Development Party (AKP) and optimism about Turkey's EU membership bid have driven markets higher in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  The lira weakened to close Tuesday at best dollar bids of 1,534,500, below the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1,510,000 point when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars and Monday's close of 1,523,000. This is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest level in more than five months. \par \par \uc2  December 3, 2003, debt fell and yields rose to 47.34 percent from 47.16. July 2, 2003 paper yielded 49.96 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The market has consolidated, taking into account the risk (of lira falls) in the coming days," said a trader. \par \par \uc2  Turkish stocks slipped 1.03 percent to close at 13,226.38 points with brokers citing worries about a possible U.S. attack on neighbouring Iraq. U.S. Deputy Defence Secretary Paul Wolfowitz visited Ankara on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the Iraq issue is back has brought a fall in the stock market. The visit has brought Iraq back onto the agenda," said Niyazi Atasoy at Ata Invest in Istanbul. \par \par \uc2  Turkish newspapers on Tuesday said the U.S. had asked Turkey to contribute troops to a possible invasion of Iraq if Baghdad fails to adhere to U.N. resolutions barring it from holding weapons of mass destruction. \par \par \uc2  Wolfowitz mentioned nothing about an official request for Turkish support at a Tuesday news conference saying "close Turkish-American cooperation" would be key to disarming Iraq voluntarily. \par \par \uc2  Turkish markets were little moved by Tuesday's data showing an 11.8 percent rise in industrial output in October compared to October 2001. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the data showed Turkey would easily exceed a four percent gross national product (GNP) growth target for 2002. \par \par \uc2  Investors also focused on November price data, published after the market close. Consumer price inflation (CPI) rose a monthly 2.9 percent in November, in line with expectations. \par \par \uc2  Turkish CPI now stands at 31.8 percent year-on-year, below an IMF-backed 35 percent target for 2002. \par \par \uc2  Trade in local markets will halt after Wednesday's morning session ahead of a public holiday to mark the end of the Muslim holy month of Ramadan. Market's reopen next week. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021203dyc300g22\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
