\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Turkey - July 12. \b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2002\par 08:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ANKARA, July 12 (Reuters) - These are the leading stories in the Turkish press on Friday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  CUMHURIYET \par \par \uc2  - President Ahmet Necdet Sezer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent Economy Minister Kemal Dervis, the torch-bearer of Turkey's $16 billion IMF pact, from resigning amid a government crisis. \par \par \uc2  FINANSAL FORUM \par \par \uc2  - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prop up the lira as Dervis announces his departure. \par \par \uc2  HURRIYET \par \par \uc2  - Dervis is now the fourth partner in Turkey's coalition government after Prime Minister Bulent Ecevit and the president persuade him to stay on to implement economic reforms. \par \par \uc2  MILLIYET \par \par \uc2  - The economy minister's swift about-turn does not mean he has abandoned a new political movement with ex-Foreign Minister Ismail Cem and ex-deputy premier Husamettin Ozkan. \par \par \uc2  RADIKAL \par \par \uc2  - Leaders of the IMF, World Bank and European Union abandon Turkey's ailing premier by canceling trips to the NATO member and EU membership candidate. \par \par \uc2  SABAH \par \par \uc2  - Cem's resignation makes breaking news on CNN and the BBC as he plans a new political force to lead Turkey to the doors of the European Union. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020712dy7c00c24\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
