\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish lira slides, traders worry at volatility. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mete Akcok \par \uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2002\par 16:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Feb 11 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira slipped on Monday to its lowest level against the dollar this year, mostly on selling from London-based banks. \par \par \uc2  The lira fell to 1,408,000 to the dollar on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -brokered spot market from Friday's 1,372,000 lira but firmed slightly to close at 1,385,000 lira. \par \par \uc2  Stocks on the main Istanbul National-100 index ended the day up 3.73 percent at 11,675.15 points as worries subsided over possible U.S. action against neighbouring Iraq, which had led markets down last week. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think it (the lira selling) has anything to do with the Iraq issue. Foreign institutions in London led the (dollar) buying. Local banks that were selling lira reacted to the (dollar's) rise and bought dollars," said one local banker. \par \par \uc2  The lira is now off the highs of some 1,296,000 to the dollar reached last week on IMF approval of a new $16 billion loan pact for \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop excessive fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that Turkish exporters say render pricing difficult, but the IMF pact limits funds the bank can inject into the market in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The busiest Turkish bills maturing on February 5, 2003 weakened to average yields of 71.75 percent from 70.33 percent. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR DANGER \par \par \uc2  Ankara has pledged to make inflation targeting a centrepiece of its monetary and fiscal policy but says fluctuations in the lira and burgeoning inflation should first subside. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the lira selling did not bode well for a year-end consumer price inflation target of 35 percent and could damage economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "This game with the dollar is a dangerous one for the year-end inflation target...The manufacturing sector as much as the financial sector cannot take this much volatility," another banker told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Investors had been unsettled by market speculation about a possible Iraqi reply to Turkish Prime Minister Bulent Ecevit's warning last week that Iraq might face U.S. strikes if it did not allow U.N. weapons inspectors back into the country. \par \par \uc2  But the local press released what they said were the contents of Iraqi President Saddam Hussein's response at the weekend. This contained none of the aggressive rhetoric rumoured last week. \par \par \uc2  Brokers said lower tension over Iraq had helped the stock market post gains, but the lira's weakness had also encouraged buying as stocks had cheapened in dollar terms. \par \par \uc2  "Total losses last week approached 30 percent taking into account the dollar's rise against the lira. Part of that fall has now been regained by this (lira buying) reaction," said Enver Gursoy of Dis Investment in Istanbul. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020211dy2b00u3n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
