\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Dervis:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Vs Overvalued Lira Needed \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2002\par 00:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Economy Minister Kemal Dervis said late Tuesday the lira is "excessively" overvalued against the dollar and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be necessary to reverse the trend. \par \par \uc2  Dervis's statement could be seen by the markets as undermining the independence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of the preconditions of the International Monetary Fund-backed economic program. \par \par \uc2  In a speech to Turkish exporters, Dervis said the "excessively valued lira will be corrected by the market." But he was quick to emphasize that monetary authorities "also need to contribute to this process, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't drift on its own." \par \par \uc2  Dervis hinted that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may come in the form of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling lira for dollars. \par \par \uc2  He added that the economic program doesn't set a ceiling for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves. "So the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the right to build up some reserves," Dervis said. \par \par \uc2  "Of course, execution and its timing is up to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an autonomous institution," he said. \par \par \uc2  After a series of crises saw the lira on a free float on February 2001, Turkey launched a new economic program backed by IMF. \par \par \uc2  The float initially worked against the lira, which shed 60% of its value against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But since October, amid signs of renewed IMF support for Turkey, the lira reversed, gaining about 20% against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  An overvalued lira increases the probability of a sharp correction, and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility could be risky to the IMF-backed economic program. \par \par \uc2  The dollar Tuesday closed at TRL1,320,000. \par \par \uc2  While the lira's free float is a key aspect of the new IMF program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already announced it can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at times of excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay, Dow Jones Newswires; 90212 2313355 selim.atalay@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020129dy1t001fu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
