\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Turk mkts slide on U.S. strikes, c.bank vigilant. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Birsen Altayli \par \uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2001\par 16:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Turkish shares, bonds and the lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Monday after U.S. and British strikes on Afghanistan overnight, but the falls were limited by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement it was ready to support the lira. The main share index in Istanbul fell four percent in early trade but clawed back some of those losses to close the day 1.31 percent lower at 7,499.02 points. \par \par \uc2  Investors said they were tracking the conflict in Afghanistan as well as Turkey's efforts to win further international lending for 2002. It says the global turmoil means it will require additional foreign aid on top of the $15.7 billion IMF-backed crisis rescue pact earmarked for this year. \par \par \uc2  "The dimensions the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes now and in the near term and the credit the IMF will give are very important," said Cem Gokkan of Anadolu Investment. \par \par \uc2  An IMF team is expected in Ankara on Wednesday for talks set to focus on Turkey's 2002 budget, government officials told Reuters on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Economy Minister Kemal Dervis said last week in Washington after talks with the fund that he saw general agreement that Turkey would need more lending to compensate for global economic turmoil after the attacks on the United States. \par \par \uc2  Investment bank Merrill Lynch said on Monday it had cut Turkish bonds to underweight from market weight in its model portfolio, citing delays in Turkey reaching an agreeement with the IMF on additional funding. \par \par \uc2  "Our market weight position of the past few weeks was not based on economic data releases and the economic outlook but on the market's anticipation of new cash from the IMF," the bank said in a research report. \par \par \uc2  The lira slid on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -brokered spot market , trading at 1,633,000 to the dollar against Friday's close of 1,580,000. That took depreciation since crisis float in February to 58 perent from Friday's 56 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  VOWS SUPPORT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday to pull the lira back from a record low of 1,652,000 to the dollar and reiterated on Monday that it was ready to step in again if needed. \par \par \uc2  "We're watching all markets very closely. We will do whatever is required," central banker Governor Sureyya Serdengecti told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Bankers estimate the size of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around $150-200 million dollars, reflecting how thin trade has become on nearly all of Turkey's financial markets as fears of the ramifications of global conflict add to domestic economic woes. \par \par \uc2  "(Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) was telling the market, I'm here and you cannot push the rate up as much as you want," said one banker, who asked not to be named. \par \par \uc2  Average yields on the benchmark March 6, 2002 bonds rose under a percentage point to 94.73 percent in very thin trade. \par \par \uc2  Turkey's treasury said on Monday it planned an auction of bills with a 91-day maturity on Tuesday as it sought to service a debt mountain swollen by the bailout of crisis-hit banks. \par \par \uc2  It gave no targeted amount for the borrowing. The treasury sold 434.7 trillion lira of 182-day bonds on October 2 at a maximum yield of 93.56 percent, above a 91 percent average borrowing the treasury targets for 2001. \par \par \uc2  The treasury faces a total 6,728.3 trillion lira ($4.2 billion) in payments on debt interest and principal in October. Of those payments, 3,850.1 trillion lira are to the market with the remainder to state institutions, state banks and banks in receivership. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011008dxa800lwy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
