\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  steps in to prop up lira. \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2001\par 14:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Oct 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday to arrest a slide in the value of the lira after it hit record lows earlier in the day, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  It was the first confirmed direct \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since the crisis in late February which forced the country to float the lira. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is putting in quotations on the market to buy lira for dollars," one banker told Reuters. Other traders also detected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  The lira responded, strengthening to 1,580,000 to the dollar on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -brokered spot market in the afternoon after reaching record lows around 1,650,000 lira. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been sliding for days, setting record after record as investors grow anxious over Economy Minister Kemal Dervis's talks with the IMF in Washington and over the likely impact for NATO member Turkey of any U.S. strikes in the Middle East. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to act to prevent "excessive" fluctuation in the value of the lira, which has lost more than half its value against the dollar since the February float. \par \par \uc2  But its room for manoeuvre is constrained by the provisions of Turkey's $15.7 billion international rescue lending package, which limits how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves can fall over time. \par \par \uc2  The bank said on Thursday its reserves had risen $1 billion to $18.925 billion in the week ending September 28, swollen by treasury deposits after a dollar and euro-denominated debt offering. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011005dxa500hka\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
