\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish lira slips, record low in sight. \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2001\par 11:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira fell sharply on Thursday raising fears that the troubled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may again slip to uncharted depths against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Turkey abandoned a managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime during a financial crisis in February and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since lost more than 50 percent of its value against the U.S. dollar as the government struggles to implement a $15.7 billion IMF rescue pact. \par \par \uc2  The lira was trading at 1,490,000 to the dollar on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -brokered spot market in mid-morning trade, down from Wednesday's 1,460,000 with a record low of 1,515,000 set last week well in sight. "Such a sudden rise (in the dollar) comes down to the fact that there are no dollar sellers," one banker said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's private banks may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and begin selling dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf in an effort to prevent the lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sinking lower. \par \par \uc2  Representatives of several major Turkish banks met with senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials last week after the lira set its record mark. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  then strengthened to around 1,420,000 lira against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources saying the banks had discussed ways to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest the slide. \par \par \uc2  The IMF pact restricts dollar sales the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can make in support of the ailing float. \par \par \uc2  Turkish shares traded on the main Istanbul National-100 index ended the morning session down 0.01 percent at 9,625.01 points after trading lower most of the morning. Yields on the most heavily traded bills maturing on March 6, 2001 rose slightly to 89.21 percent from Wednesday's 89.04 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said news of tax exemptions on bond puchases to be introduced in an effort to provoke a fall in interest rates had helped suppress any rise in yields, but stocks had not escaped the lira rot. \par \par \uc2  "This (the bond tax exemption) was not reflected in the stock market as movements in the dollar prevent this," said Alper Tavukcu of Hak Securities in Istanbul. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010823dx8n00i25\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
