\par\par \b \uc2  WRAPUP-Turkey tackling lira problems as Fischer visits. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mark Bentley \par \uc2 850 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2001\par 20:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, July 27 (Reuters) - High demand in a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond sale on Friday and an overhaul of Turkey's ailing lira borrowing programme shows poor demand for the lira, an issue which Turkey and visiting IMF number two Stanley Fischer must tackle, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  But Fischer said on Friday evening he envisaged no major changes to Turkey's $15.7 billion IMF-bail out pact, including changes to the floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime that analysts say is a major obstacle to government borrowing and business confidence. \par \par \uc2  "We see no major changes taking place in the programme," Fischer told reporters in Ankara when asked if he had discussed changes to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime with Turkey's leaders. \par \par \uc2  In a later statement, Prime Minister Bulent Ecevit said Fischer had warned him against compromising the free float. \par \par \uc2  "I conveyed our problems regarding the floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...(He) said the steps taken to abandon the floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lead to negative results. Mr Fischer said such a new evaluation will not be appropriate," Ecevit told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Ecevit said on Thursday he would discuss with Fischer ways to smooth problems caused by the free float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has looked fragile in the face of government infighting and a spat with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  LIRA BEHIND DEBT WORRIES \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the success of a Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt sale, when demand reached $2 billion for a $500 million one-year dollar and euro bonds sale, shows weakness in the lira. \par \par \uc2  And they said Turkey's abandonment on Friday of its fixed monthly domestic debt auctions, at which last week the government was forced to pay three-figure interest rates, reflected on both lira weakness and Turkey's ability to pay its domestic dues. \par \par \uc2  "There's good (\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt) demand so maybe the concern of the market is not the repayment risk of the government," said Selim Cevikel of Credit Lyonnais in Istanbul. \par \par \uc2  "The concern is that there's not much confidence in the Turkish lira, in long-term Turkish lira assets," Cevikel said. "If you do this for Turkish lira bonds for one year, you wouldn't get half of this (demand) and interest rates would probably be 95 percent." \par \par \uc2  DOMESTIC BORROWING ADDRESSED \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the major revision to the treasury's borrowing policy is a precautionary measure to keep domestic borrowing costs down amid the volatility that has plagued the lira free float in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  "Today's auction is the proof that the current exchange rate system was the major deterrent working against treasury debt auctions," said Emin Ozturk, economist at Bender Securities. \par \par \uc2  Rates in treasury lira bond auctions topped 100 percent last week during a spat between the reformist wing of the government led by economy minister Kemal Dervis and coalition nationalists seen as obstructing the IMF programme. \par \par \uc2  An auction immediately following a fateful argument between the prime minister and president in February saw interest rates soar to 144 percent from around 70 percent. \par \par \uc2  Turkish officials and the IMF agree resultant high interest rates and a growing debt load are the greatest threat to the future of the loan pact, which necessitates low interest rates to reverse a recession predicted to bring a GDP contraction of at least three percent in 2001. \par \par \uc2  Turkey hopes the abandonment of a policy of announcing a fixed monthly programme of domestic debt auctions will give it more flexibility to hold sales when conditions are favourable. \par \par \uc2  LESS FLEXIBLE FLOAT? \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the resounding success of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond sale as compared to equivalent lira bond sales may give Turkey a strong case to make alterations to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. \par \par \uc2  "It could be a tool for the government when they see Fischer," Cevikel said. \par \par \uc2  Turkey's battered lira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost nearly half of its value since its float amid financial crisis in February. A lira pegged to the dollar was the centrepiece of a now-revamped IMF-backed reform programme signed in late 1999. \par \par \uc2  But analysts do not expect Fischer and Turkey to agree on anything but minor adjustments to the free float. \par \par \uc2  "The most likely scenario is when they don't re-label policy but give more flexibility to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ozturk. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already taken measures to promote lira stability by encouraging long term lira investments through tax incentives on long-term lira deposits and bond purchases announced earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say further measures to reduce domestic debt redemptions during the rest of 2001 should also ease the pressure on the floating lira-based programme. \par \par \uc2  IMF loans, a swap of Turkish treasury debt held in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the ability of state banks to roll over their debt means Turkey only has to tap domestic debt markets for a minimum 19,000 trillion lira ($14.4 billion) this year against total debt repayments of 40,000 trillion, a treasury information note showed on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "In the rest of the year the rollover burden of the treasury is not as large as what it seemed from the redemption side," said Ozturk. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010727dx7r00xnb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
