\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish sovereign debt and European telcos led the way down ... \b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2001\par 15:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  Turkish sovereign debt and European telcos led the way down as the cost of credit protection cheapened. Tom Bergen reports. \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 27 (Reuters) - The cost of credit protection on Turkish sovereign debt fell on Tuesday as turmoil in its financial markets calmed. \par \par \uc2  Credit protection costs on European telecoms debt also fell, helped by a rebound in the sector on European stock markets, with default swap spreads tightening by midsession, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Default swaps, the most liquid part of the credit derivative market, are insurance-like tools which allow investors to juggle exposure to the risk of an issuer defaulting on an underlying loan or bond. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country's money markets for the second day running on Tuesday, providing liquidity at comparatively low interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The stock market and the Turkish lira also recovered from recent lows, contributing to more positive sentiment in the default swaps market. \par \par \uc2  "Turkey is normalising again. People are squaring positions that they weren't able to close last week," a trader with a U.S. bank said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Bid/offer spreads on Turkish one-year default swaps were quoted at 600/900, from 600/1000 on Monday. The two-year swaps were shown at 650/900, in from 700/1100. The three-year swaps had come in to 700/1000 from 800/1200 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Nonetheless, the trader added there still could be fallout if local banks began selling large quantities of their bond holdings. \par \par \uc2  "The local banks could drive the market back again. They have margin calls in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the easiest way for them to meet these is to sell their dollar bonds. A widespread sell-off would impact the default swaps market," he said. \par \par \uc2  TELECOMS STRONGER \par \par \uc2  A recovery in European technology and telecoms stocks helped to narrow spreads of default swaps on the telecoms sector on Tuesday. A trader with a major European bank said spreads had narrowed by five basis points across the board. \par \par \uc2  Five-year defaults swaps on Deutsche Telekom's debt were quoted at 150/170 from 155/175 on Monday. Vodafone was quoted at 78/82, in from around 82/86 yesterday. France Telecom was shown at 170/178, having traded at 180 on Monday. Swedish handset maker Ericsson was bid at 100 on Tuesday, narrowing from a bid/offer spread of around 107/115 yesterday. \par \par \uc2  No trading was reported in default swaps on banks or the automotive sector. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2r05flj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
