\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Turkish lira pauses, zloty firm. \b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2001\par 13:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 27 (Reuters) - The newly-floated Turkish lira steadied on Tuesday as an injection of liquidity by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped traders pause for breath, while the zloty was upbeat as the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's two-day policy meeting began. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the money market, offering cash at low interest rates to soothe markets and ease pressure on the lira, which was pushed out of its crawling peg regime last week after a political flare-up between the president and prime minister triggered a financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  The first lira-dollar deals on Tuesday's interbank market were at 970,000, a depreciation of some 29 percent since the float and marginally below late Monday levels although up from losses of 36 percent soon after it traded freely. \par \par \uc2  Investors were far from convinced that the lira was out of the woods, given the political uncertainty which clouded the prospects of an effective cure for the troubled banking sector. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, you've got a short-term containment. Interest rates have come down, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is providing liquidity and we're now in a pause, waiting for a much clearer sense of what the scale of the problem is," said Jerome Booth, head of research at Ashmore Investment Management in London. \par \par \uc2  "The thing that everybody is waiting for - mostly domestically but externally as well - is the sense that the political spat that we saw is not going to be repeated. That's very important because you can have all the policies in place but see the whole thing get out of hand again." On Tuesday, Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered overnight lira to banks at 150 percent, continuing lending at low rates. The first deals on the interbank money market were made at 100 percent, down from highs of 5,000 percent last week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also offered three-day dollar and euro lending to banks at 40 percent. \par \par \uc2  ALL EYES ON POLISH MPC Elsewhere, the zloty maintained a firm note as the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began its two-day Monetary Policy Council meeting, with many in the market expecting a rate cut of between 1.0-1.5 percentage points. \par \par \uc2  The bank has been maintaining interest rates at 19 to 23 percent - among the highest in Europe - to squeeze out inflation. But real interest rates are very high, with the consumer price index up 8.4 percent in the 12 months to January. \par \par \uc2  "The market is anticipating a rate cut of perhaps 100 to 150 basis points. Polish bonds are slightly better bid as a result, and that goes for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well," said Callum Henderson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank SSSB in London. \par \par \uc2  "Recent emerging market volatility over the last couple of days was of concern to some high-yielding markets but that seems to have calmed down," he added. \par \par \uc2  The zloty hit one-week peaks around 4.0880 to the dollar before trimming gains to around 4.0910/4.0940 by 1153 GMT, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  Against a broadly firmer euro, the zloty was trading at 3.7430/60 to the euro , down marginally on the day but still within sight of Monday's five-day peaks. \par \par \uc2  In South Africa, the rand was softer after gross domestic product growth for the fourth quarter came in at 3.2 percent, a touch below a consensus forecast for 3.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Most people were expecting something between 3.4 and 3.8 (percent growth), so 3.2 was a bit of a disappointment," said Henderson at Citibank SSSB. \par \par \uc2  "The key factors for the rand now are the trade data (due on Wednesday), and more importantly, the Anglo American/De Beers deal." \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month, mining giant Anglo American and South Africa's Oppenheimer family agreed to buy diamond miner De Beers in a $17.6 billion deal, and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders expect the transaction to generate some rand demand. \par \par \uc2  The rand was trading at around 7.7500/7.7600 to the dollar , down from around 7.72 prior to the GDP data. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2r05ap6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
