\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Sep Lira Depreciation 3.77% \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 1999\par 14:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (Dow Jones)--Dollar selling by commercial banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday afternoon, with the bank selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars. \par \par \uc2  The bank sold lira to meet the commercial banks' dollar selling demand and to adjust the lira's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  At the market's close, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing was TRL449,721 to a dollar with the euro rate at $1.0580. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said this indicates a monthly lira depreciation of a high 3.77% against the dollar/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. This is calculated on fixings from Sept. 1, compounded to the end of the month. \par \par \uc2  The indicative rate is higher than August's 3.24%. The depreciation acceleration coincides with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lowering its lira lending rate margins Wednesday to 55% and 70% from 46% and 74%. \par \par \uc2  Normally, lower margins are seen to encourage dollar buying. However the demand isn't there and traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is moving on market expectations that there will be a Standby arrangement with the International Monetary Fund this year. \par \par \uc2  Talks with a visiting IMF team started in Ankara Thursday. Initially the IMF aims to asses the damage caused by the Aug. 17 earthquake on Turkish finances. Turkish and IMF officials will meet again at the end of September and early October for detailed standby talks. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay; +90 312 466 3101; satalay@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-09-99 \par \par \uc2  1228GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9906nr8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
