\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Sparked By Banks' Dollar Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1999\par 14:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (Dow Jones)--Continuous dollar-buying by Turkish commercial banks triggered a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday afternoon, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank started buying Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars at TRL440,200. The move lowered commercial bank dollar bids to TRL439,800 and below. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the banks' dollar buying, which was stronger in morning trade, relatively subsided but still kept the lira's daily depreciation against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of $1 and EUR0.77 at above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 0.10%-0.11%. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-selling slowed the lira depreciation to the target level. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fixing was at TRL437,900 to the dollar. The bank also fixed the euro at $1.0676. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank's dollar fixing for the lira indicates a monthly lira depreciation of 3.22%, based on the fixing and compounded over 30 days. \par \par \uc2  -By Burak Bekdil; +90 312 466 3101; bbekdil@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-08-99 \par \par \uc2  1233GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8k066rh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
