\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey Central Bk -2: Monthly Lira Depreciation At 3.16% \b0\par\par\uc2 152 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1999\par 14:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Thursday afternoon, selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, in response to dollar selling for lira by commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  As a result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offers rose to TRL430,700 by the close from TRL430,300. \par \par \uc2  At the market's close, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing was TRL430,347 to a dollar and the euro/dollar rate was at $1.0192. \par \par \uc2  Traders said this indicates a lira depreciation rate of 3.16% for the month, against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket comprising $1 and EUR0.77. This is based on month-to-date lira depreciation compounded over 30 days. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank is indicating that it may raise the lira depreciation to 3.2% for July. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay; +90 212 231 3355 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-07-99 \par \par \uc2  1224GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7g05dhl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
