\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Sparked By Dollar Buying By Bks \b0\par\par\uc2 135 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 14:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (Dow Jones)--Continuous dollar buying by commercial banks triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday afternoon, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started buying Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars at TRL417,200. The move lowered dollar bids to TRL417,000 and below. Dollar bids closed Monday at TRL416,850, up from Friday's close of TRL415,200. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the lira's monthly (compounded) depreciation against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of $1 and EUR0.77 was at 3.60% before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the monthly depreciation fell back to end near the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target level of 3.24%. \par \par \uc2  -By Burak Bekdil; +90 312 466 3101; bbekdil@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-06-99 \par \par \uc2  1223GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6l04peg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
