\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Sold Lira For Dollars-Traders \b0\par\par\uc2 146 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 1999\par 14:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (Dow Jones)--Sales of dollars by commercial banks triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday afternoon, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank started selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars at TRL399,500. The move raised commercial banks offers for dollars to TRL399,900 and above. \par \par \uc2  Dollar offers closed Friday at TRL400,900, up from Thursday's close of TRL398,260. \par \par \uc2  Traders said sales of dollars in the afternoon session had slowed down the lira's monthly depreciation against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of $1 and EUR0.77 to 1.00%. With the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the lira's monthly depreciation to 3.12%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The banks often switch into lira Fridays to take advantage of weekend\par repo gains.\par    -By Burak Bekdil; +90 312 466 3101; bbekdil@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-05-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1225GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5l03z2p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
