\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Sparked By Banks' Dollar Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1999\par 14:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (Dow Jones)--Continuous dollar selling by commercial banks triggered a round of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday afternoon, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank started selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars at TRL389,250. The move raised commercial bank dollar offers to TRL389,850 and above. \par \par \uc2  Dollar offers closed Thursday at TRL390,250, down from Wednesday's close at TRL391,280. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying also raised the lira's daily depreciation against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of $1 and EUR0.77 to 0.12%, from 0.07% before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  maintains a monthly 3.70% lira depreciation against\par the dollar/euro basket.\par    -By Burak Bekdil; +90 312 466 3101; bbekdil@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-05-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1214GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5603de3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
