\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey Ctrl Bk -2: Lira Depreciation At Daily 0.11% \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 1999\par 14:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Wednesday afternoon, selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, and further slowing the lira's depreciation rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came before the market's close and moved the dollar offers to TRL391,500 from TRL391,400. \par \par \uc2  The bank's fixing was at TRL391,283 with the euro rate at $1.0669, and indicated a monthly depreciation rate of 3.6% against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket comprising of $1 and euro 0.77. \par \par \uc2  This is below Tuesday's indicative rate of 3.7% and below Monday's 3.9%. \par \par \uc2  Traders are eying the depreciation rate to adjust their lira funding costs as positions are funded by short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the indicative lira depreciation rate calculations vary among banks, as some see depreciation at 3.1%. \par \par \uc2  Overall, the consensus is that the daily lira depreciation rate against the basket is at 0.10% to 0.11%. \par \par \uc2  Traders said it's still early to predict a monthly trend and the bank levels will be watched further. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay; +90 212 231 3355; satalay@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-05-99 \par \par \uc2  1251GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5503dvs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
