\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey Central Bk -2: Slows Lira Depreciation To 3.75% \b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 1999\par 14:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market Tuesday afternoon, selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, slowing the lira's depreciation rate. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank might be giving the message that it won't accelerate the lira's depreciation rate. \par \par \uc2  Following Monday's higher-than-expected April inflation data, market participants were worried that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might accelerate lira depreciation, thus further raising the funding cost for lira positions. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came shortly before the market's close, when best offers were around TRL392,450, and carried offers to TRL392,700 and higher at the close. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar at TRL392,470 for Wednesday. This indicates a monthly lira depreciation rate of 3.75% against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket comprising $1 and EUR0.77, traders said, down from Tuesday's indicative rate of 3.9%. \par \par \uc2  The lira's depreciation rate in April was 4.1% against the basket. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 04-05-99 \par \par \uc2  1243GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5403esq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
