\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Sparked By Banks' Dollar Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 118 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 1999\par 14:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Dollar-selling by commercial banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday afternoon, with the bank selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the lira's depreciation rate to a monthly 4% against the dollar/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the commercial banks' dollar-selling continues as they are switching to lira positions, because of hopes of political stability after Sunday's elections. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday the dollar closed at TRL385,954, up from Tuesday's close of TRL384,246. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay; 90 212 231 3355; satalay@ap.org. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-04-99 \par \par \uc2  1217GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4l02y0n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
