\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Sells Lira For Dollars In Morning Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 1999\par 13:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Dollar-selling by commercial banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning trading session Thursday, with the bank selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the lira's depreciation rate to a daily 0.14% to 0.15% against the dollar and euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-week repurchase securities auction where banks received TRL260 trillion of securities with an average compounded rate of 146.44%, against demand of TRL327.5 trillion. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market was balanced between dollar buyers and sellers. However, they added this balance could tip in either direction in afternoon trading, inviting further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 1100 GMT, the dollar was quoted at TRL372,880, up from TRL372,690 earlier and up from from Friday's close of TRL369,200. \par \par \uc2  The market is trading for the first time since Friday, following the Bayram religious holiday. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay +90 212 231 3355; satalay@ap.org. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-04-99 \par \par \uc2  1127GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826d