\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buys Lira For Dlrs In Afternoon Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 131 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 13:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Dollar-selling by commercial banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in afternoon trade Monday, with the bank buying Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the lira's depreciation rate to the regular 0.13% against the dollar/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was brief and didn't quite meet the dollar selling demand by banks. They expect another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the market's close at 1300 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Around 1223 GMT dollar was quoted at TRL366,280, up from Friday's close of 364,000. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay; +90 212 231 3355; satalay@ap.org. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-03-99 \par \par \uc2  1234GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3m0282p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
