\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Sparked By Banks' Dollar-Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 152 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 1999\par 14:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (Dow Jones)--Persistent dollar-buying by commercial banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in afternoon trading Monday, and buy Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started when bank bids were at TRL339,390, and it caused bids to fall to TRL339,200 and under. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet the dollar-buying demand and slow the lira's depreciation rate. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the lira's daily depreciation against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of $1 and EUR0.77 was at 0.16%-0.17% before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The depreciation slowed to 0.15% after the bank sold dollars. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is maintaining a monthly lira depreciation of 4.50%. \par \par \uc2  -By Burak Bekdil; +90 312 466 3101; bbekdil@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-02-99 \par \par \uc2  1330GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2800zqs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
