\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  lira ends easier vs dlr after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1999\par 15:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira ended weaker at around 335,300 per dollar on Wednesday, versus Monday's 335,000, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold lira for dollars in late trade to guard its lira depreciation target for the sixth day in a row. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the lira's daily depreciation rate firmed to 0.15 percent, from 0.12 percent levels before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank trade was mostly balanced during the day. But minor dollar sales by foreigners prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell lira for dollars towards the close," one banker said. \par \par \uc2  Bankers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its daily lira depreciation target to 0.15 percent in the first days of February from an average 0.13-0.14 percent in January. \par \par \uc2  "This may be an indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects January wholesale inflation (WPI) at least above four percent according preliminary data in hand," one banker said. \par \par \uc2  Market forecasts are seeing 3.5-4.5 percent for January WPI, showed a Reuters poll earlier this week. The inflation data will be announced at around 1430 GMT by State Statistics Office. \par \par \uc2  Turkish banks have been selling dollars for lira since the beginning of the last week to widen their short foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions. \par \par \uc2  Bankers say some foreign investors have also switched from hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Turkish lira instruments, after earlier concerns linked to the Brazil devaluation faded. \par \par \uc2  ((Mete Akcok, Istanbul newsroom, +90-212-275 3703, fax +90-212-267 2137, istanbul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv230594p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
