\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Meet Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1999\par 15:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Dollar-buying by commercial banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday afternoon, with the bank buying Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet the demand and to slow the lira's depreciation rate. \par \par \uc2  The bank maintained a daily depreciation rate of 0.15%, corresponding to a monthly 4.2% to 4.5% decline against the dollar/Euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the recent alteration of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket from dollar/Deutsche mark to dollar/Euro on Jan. 1 has also altered the way they calculate the lira's depreciation rate, and there's no uniform market formula yet for the calculation. \par \par \uc2  As a result, monthly depreciation rate calculations from individual traders differ, ranging between 4.2% and 4.5%. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the dollar closed at TRL321,900, up from Thursday's close of TRL321,750. \par \par \uc2  Friday, markets will close until Jan. 25 for the religious Bayram holiday. \par \par \uc2  Money markets will be open from 0800 GMT to 1130 GMT Monday Jan. 18 and, all day Friday Jan. 22. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay +90 212 231 3355; satalay@ap.org. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1404GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1f00cvn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw1