\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish Mkts Expect Another Nervous Day On Brazil Woes \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 09:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Turkish markets are expected to witness another nervous and volatile day Thursday amid worries about the Brazilian economy and its potential effects on emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  Turkish bonds and stocks slid and lira liquidity was used to buy dollars after the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Gustavo Franco resigned and Brazil widened the trading band for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the real - against the dollar Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Turkish demand for dollars prompted at least two major \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  where the bank bought lira for dollars. Traders estimate the bank may have sold about $750 million Wednesday and see half that amount being sold by the bank Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Around 1025 GMT and 25 minutes into trading, the IMKB-100 was at 2545.38 points, up 97.85 points or 4% from Wednesday's close at 2447.53 points. \par \par \uc2  Bond rates were at 128% to 130% range, down from early 132% to 134% range. The decline is seen as a correction, following Wednesday's 16 point surge towards 140%. \par \par \uc2  The dollar demand continues with the dollar at 322,050 Turkish lira (TRL), up from Wednesday's TRL320,200. Traders said the rate indicates a monthly lira depreciation of 4.28% against the dollar/Euro basket and the bank is likely to lower it Thursday to 4.15% through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying lira for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Participants said Thursday's buys won't be paid for until Jan. 25 when the religious Bayram holiday ends and this might encourage some selective buying at bargain prices. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0847GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1e00b6n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
