\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Dlr Demand Revives With Brazil \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 14:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Concerns about Brazil's economy triggered a heavy outflow from Turkish markets Wednesday, as bonds and stocks slid and lira liquidity was used to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  The dollar demand prompted at least two major \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars. \par \par \uc2  At the market's close at 1200 GMT, the dollar was at TRL320,200, down from TRL322,550 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its monthly lira depreciation rate of 4.3% against the dollar/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  Anxiety over developments in Brazil has been gathering this week. Tuesday saw a 7.6% fall in the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's Bovespa index, leading drops in other regional and emerging market exchanges. \par \par \uc2  Brazil also suffered a net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflow of $1.2 billion Tuesday, much faster than the recent daily rate of $100-$200 million. \par \par \uc2  This was compounded early in Wednesday's session by reports, later confirmed, that \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Gustavo Franco had resigned. He will be replaced by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy director Francisco Lopes. \par \par \uc2  Brazil also widened the dollar's trading band against the real, but traders remain fearful of devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Turkey's depreciation rate might increase as jitters over Brazil are seen continuing Thursday. At the end of trading Friday, Turkish markets will start the religious Bayram holiday until Jan 25. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money markets will be open half day Monday Jan. 15 until 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay +90 212 231 3355; satalay@ap.org. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1354GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1d00a1f\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Turkey near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brd